KZ3 patch 2066 (RSX pass 64, diagnostic): LD_DRAW_DUMP_SURF=<hex colour offset> limits the per-draw target dump
(LD_DRAW_DUMP, LD_DRAW_DUMP_EVERY) and the LD_DRAW_INPUTS selection to the draws into one surface, counted on their
own (the n-th draw into that surface in the frame). In a level the shadow passes before the G-buffer pass draw a
different number of times from frame to frame and run to run (K2: the G-buffer started at draw 1528 in one run and
2073 in another at the same view), so a frame-relative index cannot name a G-buffer draw ahead of the run; the
surface-relative one can. With the filter the dumps start at the first frame that began inside the
RSX_DRAW_CSV_GATE window (no partial frame) and LD_DRAW_INPUTS frame 0 is that same frame, so the target before each
draw and the draw's inputs come from one frame. LD_DRAW_INPUTS entries may be ranges (a-b, at most 16 entries).
Without LD_DRAW_DUMP_SURF nothing changes. Log: [draw-dump] surface filter <offset>.

